h2 class=3D"corner-header">=0D=0A                              <img src=3D"=
https://assets.codepen.io/t-1/chriscorner.png" style=3D"width: 65px; border=
-radius: 4px;" /> Chris=E2=80=99 Corner=0D=0A                            </=
h2>=0D=0A                            <p class=3D"corner-intro">A collection=
 of web design and development news and thoughts from CodePen's own Chris C=
oyier.</p>=0D=0A                          </mj-raw>=0D=0A                  =
        <p>I=E2=80=99ve had View Transitions on the mind a little bit after=
 experimenting with using them to <a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/=
f/a/9Iwh3LUZviP4Dh88GnRClg~~/AABEfhA~/IL03uHLBoH8dFnNIGcGJKPYYZZH6vyveXS08H=
Q9Oym6156tdJLOSPVQxTwu8rTNB-q6HkOj3lHO5TBxXs4QLFb3wqh-OXjQxR19ENIDHR8AMaR5i=
NYdEZQd7wiVOOySRYfMe4CiuMntcDaBHPYy-TZ1_rzawYuw5EhsgUWdedWter0EKXM71oggnygr=
PCmMJ">move the focus ring around the page</a>. I found that pretty satisfy=
ing, except the part where I was binding events to the tab key myself and k=
eeping track of =E2=80=9Cfocusable=E2=80=9D elements. I know better, as tha=
t kind of thing is always best left to the browser. I was just checking whe=
ther it was possible to animate that focus style from place to place, since=
 it wasn=E2=80=99t really =E2=80=9Cthe same=E2=80=9D element (and arguably =
not an element at all). It is totally possible.</p>=0D=0A<p>But then I=E2=
=80=99m glad Kilian Valkhof chimed in with his <a href=3D"https://go.sparkp=
ostmail2.com/f/a/Px7y9rbOns7D-5Tm2BtoLg~~/AABEfhA~/w52pWkBri_79l4-UDdiVbQKZ=
u7Kv_sM3NEvIuKPNZTC4yBgnyj2obo8C33kTGIsm1O8-9UonVbNHZ3dR7b_FyMvErsO3i1vrHJX=
IYTDp7X0O0K1XiKNkWU05Ev3E7WdRAJ2Oo2kSf7shST-vKrcv8Z6HWM47oyk_oVYjjpseV0oXuU=
HdzLFegKR0K64zi2RT">CSS-only floating focus with anchor positioning</a>, wh=
ich pulls it off without needing any JavaScript at all. I guess I still pro=
ved it can be done with View Transitions, but certainly <a href=3D"https://=
go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/ltgsaMUfhKthT07pi2fdbw~~/AABEfhA~/fRzhx4PUxKJKDJC=
DeJxMfob4JPe8esU1M1lDbSg3pep41vPBrsFHBV5p_oan93QbN0eIzNEKrGL4-DOW4llc9WHmTr=
TNHb7XSC8KKFLZ_MS6F9I5D_qTf9QQmx5u1v39lT6eODjN3xvKJ-rjqcjm8Q~~">Kilian=E2=
=80=99s demo</a> is much cleaner. Jealous! I should have thought of that.</=
p>=0D=0A<p>In my own last demo, I noticed something about the CSS styles I =
was playing with to control the animations.</p>=0D=0A<pre><code class=3D"cs=
s">/* movement */=0D=0A::view-transition-group(focus-ring) {=0D=0A}=0D=0A=
=0D=0A/* resizing */=0D=0A::view-transition-old(focus-ring),=0D=0A::view-tr=
ansition-new(focus-ring) {=0D=0A}=0D=0A</code></pre>=0D=0A<p>I put those co=
mment labels there, as I happen to notice that if you changed the <code>ani=
mation-duration</code> on them to exaggerate things, it seemed the <code>vi=
ew-transition-group</code> was in charge of the moving and the other two we=
re in charge of the morphing of one shape to another. I honestly don=E2=80=
=99t even get it. I emailed <a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/rQ=
bd-V76lOf_HITowXU1Bw~~/AABEfhA~/Ew3kwq2gr-4NzIXtg6qnoGOtDYK4XWGmD_J8xh7elv2=
hcaUtQipdpVVcd10Nq4a6fCkfmf5j6_Cg9NeESdyO1TECdsKDWgaJfLyzeFCP8ezfRc4N11nBWN=
iwPLvh3sOB">Cyd</a> to see if she can explain it haha, we=E2=80=99ll see if=
 we get that blog post someday.</p>=0D=0A<p>I do know that you can see the =
pseduo element tree of View Transitions stuff in the DOM (via Chrome DevToo=
ls) as the animations happen.</p>=0D=0A<img src=3D"https://production-codep=
en-email-assets.codepenassets.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=3D600,quality=3D90,fo=
rmat=3Dauto/codepen-spark/view-trainsitions-dom.png" alt=3D"Chrome DevTools=
 showing the pseudo-element tree of a view transition. " width=3D"350"/>=0D=
=0A<p>That=E2=80=99s nice, as you can click on them and see what=E2=80=99s =
what.</p>=0D=0A<p>But notice how they are all children of the <code>&lt;htm=
l&gt;</code> element=3F</p>=0D=0A<p>Well, ultimately, that=E2=80=99s becaus=
e we call <code>document.startViewTransition()</code>. Document. That=E2=80=
=99s <code>&lt;html&gt;</code>. That=E2=80=99s required for now, but there =
is <a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/G3C4xBDMPdp7QFw-IIy3bA~~/AA=
BEfhA~/J-eHWCQQlNeLnGq-oumOSG0ckX8uSH2ccJED5SxJ6-eJip-BTRFaD-0IJEOZ_essWlGn=
NCTPCTTO1e2wA9deydg0GwkkB0V280717p0JcSjM_TAXSDLX9bT3oxP692nS7RutCrqinUP6Ic0=
7K_v_-DQbCsVbUdycZUHMxZpTAwEdf0KhuYLIDRERFA2tLaoe">a proposal</a> to be abl=
e to call <code>startViewTransition</code> from other elements, meaning it =
would be =E2=80=9Cscoped=E2=80=9D down to that element. This allows, for on=
e thing, multiple View Transitions to run at once, which is impossible righ=
t now. It=E2=80=99s <a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/JUXBO5yQL4=
VDUscQDB2VPQ~~/AABEfhA~/fZ6fIlV1EFm1Riy1dX8dLKZxPU5P0eaJ65xZx008g4L9_itnWl5=
SJ1ju5mf5-XxJjEJIrW_p8Zwr09H9fbBmo9XAQv0BHzT34XCI8WRblw8W3JRtkoYRUtURW5M7dU=
AzbpU2ju_5xpJyn1ncObZoZXSYNzgMch-7RIrhf4DWzxjnd6zow6dg7LvxtqMnF76O">ready f=
or testing</a>, Chrome says.</p>=0D=0A<p>The part I like the most about sco=
ped view transitions is that that psuedo element tree we looked at above is=
 placed within the element you call it on, and that element might have some=
thing like <code>overflow: hidden</code> on it, and it will actually be res=
pected, as <a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/m6hT-ZlHltxnjw1mD4O=
Elg~~/AABEfhA~/lnrUWCZuUeV9uIZ2HjUFudAnGkOb1FZpLVeoAdXpOz8uhjyRwv_n_DOSL4lk=
VNA090HTzXOTrL-AEoiSVRu5fZhu4rXvmCXZH6DTQPcn8LT_U5x07K8ZdOa-Hhqb_WmKQI71-8o=
1VwYnCXK2f4BBew~~">Bramus=E2=80=99 demo clearly demonstrates</a>. It=E2=80=
=99s nice to be able to experiment and understand how these things work. Th=
anks, CodePen.</p>=0D=0A<p>Speaking of Bramus, he=E2=80=99s got a <a href=
=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/tc6jetj7sP2Y-dlfChE6xA~~/AABEfhA~/AU3=
2u9F3iAv5iNfWKW9efY7whK9YOQTB_IKXV-LjJYpk2SJ80OKxc2YTAqxCLYPTHcSD8uaPCsZe3t=
IPKuxfBZ8sixeg6EbvophVCLqz9Gvm0FMamPBE3NQxwcvm-kfiArGW6iY0gAO6e5phQZKnFA~~"=
>View Transitions Toolkit</a> he=E2=80=99s put out. I haven=E2=80=99t playe=
d with it yet, but it looks like it=E2=80=99s got some real practical goodi=
es like detecting support and dealing with the fallback structure and auto-=
naming functions. But the feature I=E2=80=99d probably use the most is the =
ability to scrub through the animations. I gave it a shot and found it a li=
ttle complex to set up, relying on some fairly complex helper functions tha=
t aren=E2=80=99t a part of the package itself, but <a href=3D"https://go.sp=
arkpostmail2.com/f/a/9Csl4i9Tjrc4iKyYgkIOwQ~~/AABEfhA~/ChjT5TwHZ9BC9LulcYZC=
LoJ_cgaVt9bjzQ93vOWIuEIROHQ9MwroQgIniSZxGCVvUs5pCx9nyLguScjJz-Flikeme8Ml89P=
omIUCMB_dBjmEmQrIBSvI7VNMzDOBk-CbUYxwByhhZ9Fl2afnB55rmh6qVEopjv_w_RjKQQIW2f=
JZW6msC0whNj7AMgHQZePi">I did get a demo working</a>.</p>=0D=0A<img src=3D"=
